% ============================================================================
% syllable-segmentation.query.adj — a worked recall over the literacy
% syllable-segmentation library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what two syllables does
% 'peanut' break into?": it states no linguistics fact — it only `import`s
% the grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?`
% against the `syllable_segmentation` rows and returns the two syllables +
% the table's source/locator/trust. The fourth query runs the relation
% BACKWARD (bind the two syllables `sun`/`set`, recall the word they came
% from). A word this source does not demonstrate segmenting is not in the
% table, so a recall on it abstains honestly — the engine never invents a
% segmentation.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli syllable-segmentation.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "syllable-segmentation.adj"

? syllable_segmentation(peanut, $S1, $S2)      % expect pea, nut
? syllable_segmentation(laptop, $S1, $S2)      % expect lap, top
? syllable_segmentation($Word, sun, set)       % expect sunset — reverse recall
? syllable_segmentation(pretzel, $S1, $S2)     % expect abstain — not one of the four words this source demonstrates
